    "text": "Fed Flags Overspending Fears as Invisible Payments Soar\nBy PYMNTS,\n7 hours agoFrictionless commerce has increasingly been the holy grail of online and in-store commerce. Embedded payments, integrated into platforms, are visible, and require a moment of click-through and interaction. Invisible payments happen in the background, with nary a hint of consumer effort. Uber is the typical archetype, as the transaction happens at the end of the trip, with the charges levied automatically.",
